  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>⇌</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is obtained by reversing the reaction<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>⇌</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and then multiplying it by the factor '2'. Hence the equilibrium constant <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mtext>K'</mtext></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math> for this reaction is given by<br /><math> <mrow>  <mtext>K'=</mtext><msup>   <mrow>    <mrow><mo>(</mo>     <mrow>      <mfrac>       <mtext>1</mtext>       <mtext>K</mtext>      </mfrac>      </mrow>    <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow>   <mtext>2</mtext>  </msup>  <mo>=</mo><msup>   <mrow>    <mrow><mo>(</mo>     <mrow>      <mfrac>       <mn>1</mn>       <mrow>        <mn>0.44</mn></mrow>      </mfrac>      </mrow>    <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow>   <mn>2</mn>  </msup>  <mo>=</mo><mn>5.16</mn></mrow></math>"
  }
